  "outcome": "O9",
  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "O9",
    "direction": "improves",
    "magnitude": "minor",
    "time_horizon": "this-parliament",
    "confidence": "moderate",
    "plain": "Scrapping the Vagrancy Act removes a law that criminalises people for being homeless or begging, ending a source of criminal records that blocked access to employment and support. The improvement is real but narrow \u2014 equal-treatment gains come mainly from removing this specific criminalisation, not from broader democratic rights reform.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether replacement legislation targeting 'organised begging and trespassing' reintroduces similar discriminatory enforcement against homeless individuals in practice.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy commits to immediately scrapping the Vagrancy Act.",
