      "notes": "Verdict is well-constructed and passes all checks. The Vagrancy Act repeal is squarely within O9 scope (equal treatment, criminalisation based on status). Claims are appropriately tiered: E8 is correctly marked 'projected' despite being a government confirmation (the repeal hadn't yet occurred at time of writing). E13 (homeless.org.uk) is an advocacy source but is used only to support a factual claim about legal consequences of convictions, which is verifiable and not the sole basis for the verdict. E14 (crisis.org.uk) similarly labelled advocacy but used narrowly. The E4 claim about hidden women is weakly connected to O9 equal-treatment but not overstated. Magnitude 'minor' is appropriately conservative. The biggest_unknown about replacement legislation is genuine and flagged. No party-blind issues, no false balance, no lever leakage."
